       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of ibuprofen for adults (3,200 mg/day under medical supervision). A single 1,600 mg dose is also twice the usual maximum single dose of 800 mg. That puts the patient at serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 3 times daily** (2,400 mg/day), a common prescription anti-inflammatory dose\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the maximum daily dose\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, every 6 hours** for analgesia\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily or 800 mg twice daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll flag it in the order note. I'd still advise confirming it with pharmacy first. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
