       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the specialist's recommendation or the chart note. A dose of 6,400 mg/day is also well beyond any established dosing range for ibuprofen. Higher doses add no extra anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect, and they sharply raise the risk of GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. The risk is high enough that I'd want a second check before it goes in.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **I can enter the maximum labeled dose now.** That's ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily (3,200 mg/day), and I can add a note that the specialist has recommended a higher dose, pending review.\n- **Pharmacy and the specialist can confirm the dose first.** I'd suggest asking them to document the rationale, the intended duration, and the monitoring plan, such as GI protection, renal function, and blood pressure. If the order is then entered with their sign-off, it will carry a proper audit trail.\n- **A different agent may fit better.** If standard ibuprofen dosing failed, the specialist may want to consider another NSAID or a different drug class.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter the order."
